[{"category":"section","location":"api/#api","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Cache-types","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Cache types"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Mapping-functions","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Mapping functions"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Utilities","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Utilities"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#Cached.DictCache","page":"API Reference","text":"DictCache()\n\nA cache that stores items in memory using a Dict. Items are not persisted and are lost when the Julia process ends.\n\nExamples\n\nusing Cached\n\ncache = DictCache()\ncmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:5)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Cached.DictCache"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#Cached.FileCache","page":"API Reference","text":"FileCache(dir::AbstractString; clear = false, gitignore = true)\n\nA cache that persists items to disk inside dir using Julia's Serialization module. Each item is stored as a separate file named by the hash of its key. Items are also cached in memory after first access to avoid redundant deserialization.\n\nArguments\n\ndir: Path to the directory where cached files will be stored.\nclear: Remove and recreate the directory if it exists (default: false).\ngitignore: Create a .gitignore file in the cache directory ignoring all contents (default: true).\n\nExamples\n\nusing Cached\n\ncache = FileCache(\"my_cache\")\ncmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:5)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Cached.FileCache"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#Cached.SQLiteCache","page":"API Reference","text":"SQLiteCache(path::AbstractString; clear = false)\n\nA cache that persists items to a SQLite database file at path using Julia's Serialization module. Items are also cached in memory after first access to avoid redundant deserialization.\n\nSQLite's WAL mode is not enabled by default, but the busy timeout is set to 1000 ms, making SQLiteCache tolerant of brief contention from concurrent processes.\n\nArguments\n\npath: Path to the SQLite database file to create or open.\nclear: Remove any existing database file at path before creating (default: false).\n\nExamples\n\nusing Cached\n\ncache = SQLiteCache(\"my_cache.sqlite\")\ncmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:5)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Cached.SQLiteCache"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Cached.cmap","page":"API Reference","text":"cmap(f, cache::AbstractCache, c; showprogress = true, kwargs...) -> Vector\ncmap(f, cache::AbstractCache, c1, c2, ...; kwargs...) -> Vector\n\nMap f over collection c, storing and retrieving results from cache. Each input element is hashed with Base.hash to form the cache key, so any previously cached result for a given input value is reused without calling f again — even across separate Julia sessions when using a persistent backend.\n\nThe multi-collection form cmap(f, cache, c1, c2, ...) zips the collections and calls f(x1, x2, ...) for each tuple of elements.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Function to apply to each element.\ncache: An AbstractCache (e.g. DictCache, FileCache, SQLiteCache).\nc: Collection of inputs.\nshowprogress: Display a progress bar (default: true).\nkwargs...: Forwarded to ProgressMeter.progress_map.\n\nExamples\n\nusing Cached\n\ncache = SQLiteCache(\"results.sqlite\")\n\n# First call: computes and caches all values\nresults = cmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:10)\n\n# Second call: all results are retrieved from cache\nresults = cmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:10)\n\n# Multi-collection form\ncmap((x, y) -> x + y, cache, 1:5, 6:10)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Cached.cmap"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Cached.pcmap","page":"API Reference","text":"pcmap(f, p::AbstractWorkerPool, cache::AbstractCache, c; kwargs...) -> Vector\npcmap(f, cache::AbstractCache, c; kwargs...) -> Vector\npcmap(f, [p], cache::AbstractCache, c1, c2, ...; kwargs...) -> Vector\n\nParallel version of cmap. Maps f over collection c using the worker pool p, caching results in cache. Each input is hashed with Base.hash — cached values are returned immediately without dispatching to a worker.\n\nWhen called without a worker pool, p defaults to CachingPool(workers()). If the pool contains no remote workers (or only the current process), f is executed locally without any remote dispatch.\n\nThe multi-collection form zips the collections and calls f(x1, x2, ...).\n\nArguments\n\nf: Function to apply to each element.\np: Worker pool (optional; defaults to CachingPool(workers())).\ncache: An AbstractCache (e.g. SQLiteCache).\nc: Collection of inputs.\ndistributed: Whether to dispatch to remote workers (default: true). Set to false to run locally while still using the cache.\nbatch_size: Number of items per remote call. Currently only 1 is supported.\non_error: Called with (x, e) when f(x) throws. Forwarded to Distributed.pmap; nothing means errors propagate immediately.\nretry_delays: Iterable of delays (seconds) for automatic retry on failure.\nretry_check: Predicate (state, e) -> Bool controlling whether a retry should be attempted. Used together with retry_delays.\nshowprogress: Display a progress bar (default: true).\n\nExamples\n\nusing Cached\nusing Distributed\n\naddprocs(4)\n\ncache = SQLiteCache(\"results.sqlite\")\n\n# Uncached items are computed on workers; cached items are returned immediately\nresults = pcmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:100)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Cached.pcmap"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Cached.wrap_cache","page":"API Reference","text":"wrap_cache(f, cache::AbstractCache) -> Function\n\nReturn a new single-argument function that wraps f with caching via cache. On the first call with a given input x, f(x) is computed and stored. Subsequent calls with the same x return the cached value without calling f.\n\nThe input is keyed by Base.hash(x).\n\nArguments\n\nf: The function to wrap. Must accept a single argument.\ncache: An AbstractCache used to store and retrieve results.\n\nExamples\n\nusing Cached\n\ncache = SQLiteCache(\"results.sqlite\")\nsquare = wrap_cache(x -> x^2, cache)\n\nsquare(4)  # computed and cached\nsquare(4)  # returned from cache\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Cached.wrap_cache"},{"category":"section","location":"#Cached.jl","page":"Home","text":"Cached.jl provides cmap and pcmap — drop-in replacements for Base.map and Distributed.pmap that transparently cache results. On the first call each input is hashed and the result stored in the chosen backend; on any subsequent call the cached value is returned immediately without re-running the function.","title":"Cached.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","text":"using Cached\n\n# Pick a backend — results persist across Julia sessions\ncache = SQLiteCache(\"results.sqlite\")\n\n# First call: every element is computed and stored\nresults = cmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:100)\n\n# Second call: everything is already cached, no computation\nresults = cmap(x -> x^2, cache, 1:100)","title":"Quick start"},{"category":"section","location":"#Cache-backends","page":"Home","text":"Type Persists? Best for\nDictCache No Deduplication within a single run\nFileCache Yes (files) Large objects, any serializable value\nSQLiteCache Yes (SQLite) Many small/medium items, concurrent access","title":"Cache backends"},{"category":"section","location":"#Parallel-mapping","page":"Home","text":"using Cached, Distributed\naddprocs(4)\n\ncache = SQLiteCache(\"results.sqlite\")\nresults = pcmap(x -> expensive_fn(x), cache, 1:1000)\n\nSee the API Reference for full documentation of all types and functions.","title":"Parallel mapping"}]
